WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.658
JEN: This week we're
talking about BigQuery, ML,

00:00:02.658 --> 00:00:03.450
and the Speed Read.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.720
I'm Jen, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.970
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.150
BigQuery's been adding so
many capabilities lately,

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.900
it can be hard to keep up.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.170
Thankfully, this
post captures it all.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.790
From a super-sized
streaming quota

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.880
to built-in support for
Federated Cloud SQL Queries,

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.610
find out what's new in BigQuery
and how you can try these out

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.043
for yourself.

00:00:25.043 --> 00:00:26.460
Have you seen
what's possible when

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.090
you combine the best of
BigQuery and Cloud AI Platform?

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:33.300
A great place to start is
ML forecasting-- a business

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.510
critical challenge when
dealing with time series data.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.220
With this code-packed
guide, you'll

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.900
see how the
framework in BigQuery

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.350
can be used to help with
all sorts of predictions.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.150
While you're at it,
see how BigQuery

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.810
can help you create models
for one more difficult task--

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.470
patent landscaping.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.530
At Google, we're
sharing a methodology

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.810
that uses Python and
BigQuery to allow

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:58.470
you to easily access patent
data and generate automated

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.790
landscapes.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.950
Read our guide, then
grab the code from GitHub

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.700
and start mapping your own.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.210
Looking for a quicker way to
keep up with hot cloud topics?

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.400
The "Google Cloud
Blog" is the new home

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.920
for the "Speed Read" by
Quentin Hardy, a "New York

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.710
Times" editor with decades of
experience observing the tech

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:16.850
sector.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:18.320
Quentin believes
we have a tendency

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.540
to over-complicate
technological change,

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.330
and he's here to put
things into perspective.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.940
Check out the "Speed Read" and
stay tuned to the "Google Cloud

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.145
Blog" for more posts.

00:01:28.145 --> 00:01:30.020
If you want to read
about these announcements

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.610
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.290
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:36.090
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:38.980
We'll see you in the cloud.

